---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How we verify | Detroit Bakery"
  description="Our sourcing rules, what we will and will not publish, how we handle unknowns and conflicting information, and how often we re-check."
>
  <section class="wrap narrow">
    <h1>How we verify</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The only thing this site has to offer is that its facts are true and current. So the
      rules that produce those facts are worth stating plainly.
    </p>

    <h2>Where facts come from</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>The bakery's own website, ordering page or menu. This is our primary source for hours, addresses, prices, lead times and policies.</li>
      <li>Direct confirmation from the bakery by phone or email.</li>
      <li>The bakery's own social accounts, for closures, hiatus announcements and seasonal items.</li>
      <li>Named local journalism, for cultural and historical context only. Never for an operational fact.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      We do not take listing content from Google Maps or Yelp. Their terms do not permit
      it, and a directory built on someone else's data is not worth reading anyway.
    </p>

    <h2>Unknown means unknown</h2>
    <p>
      Every optional detail is recorded as confirmed yes, confirmed no, or unknown. If we
      have not confirmed something, the page says so rather than leaving you to assume.
      A blank is never a quiet no. This is the difference between a filter you can trust
      and one you cannot.
    </p>

    <h2>When sources disagree</h2>
    <p>
      We do not average and we do not pick a favourite. We either leave the claim out or
      state it with the uncertainty attached, and we flag it for a direct check.
    </p>

    <h2>What we will not publish</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Invented hours, prices, lead times, phone numbers or descriptions. Not once, not to fill a gap.</li>
      <li>Ratings or review counts. We do not collect reviews, so we do not display them or mark them up for search engines.</li>
      <li>Photographs we do not have permission to use. If a profile has no photo, that is why.</li>
      <li>Claims that a bakery is safe for a specific allergy. We report what the bakery says about its own recipes and tell you to ask them directly.</li>
      <li>A "best of" ranking without a stated method. We do not sell position and we do not pretend to a verdict we have not earned.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How often we re-check</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every profile shows the date a person last checked it. That is a real date, not the date the site was last deployed.</li>
      <li>Reported errors: within a week.</li>
      <li>Hours, prices and lead times: quarterly.</li>
      <li>Everything: twice a year.</li>
      <li>Seasonal detail such as paczki pricing is either refreshed or removed each year, never left to rot.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Closures</h2>
    <p>
      A bakery that closes comes off the live list promptly, because a directory that
      sends you to a shuttered storefront has failed at its only job. Where a closure is
      worth recording we keep an accurate note rather than quietly deleting the page.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
